# Source trees homelab coordinates. Fields: name|path|remote|deploy|agent-push
#   deploy      how the tree reaches a host. Two hosts since 26 Sep 2026 (ADR
#               0010): arcade-box has the only CI agent, so every pipeline-staged
#               edge lands there; the Z840 (llm-box) has none. Which host each
#               tree reaches is in the comment above its row.
#                 buildkite    its own pipeline stages it and something on the
#                              host applies it (ac-host: queue-prod + the 03:00
#                              build, on arcade-box; homelab: queue-closure +
#                              homelab-deploy, on arcade-box -- the Z840's
#                              closure is switched by hand from a pushed sha)
#                 environment  as a flox environment (ADR 0009): its pipeline
#                              stages a sha (agent-hub) or a FloxHub generation
#                              (home-arcade) and <tenant>-environment-pull on
#                              the host that runs the tenant applies it. On a
#                              host with no agent the tenant's own poll timer
#                              does the staging from GitHub's commit status
#                              (ADR 0010 amendment, homelab-ygc.14). Nothing of
#                              the tree is in homelab's closure, and bump-lock
#                              is not involved
#                 none         nothing carries it
#   agent-push  may an agent push this remote unattended, on green gates? ("yes" or "ask")
ac-host|/home/nixos/src/ac-host|git@github.com:imkarrer/ac-host|buildkite|yes
# homelab: deploy=buildkite as of ADR 0006; since ADR 0008 (15 Sep) the
# pipeline stages a rev and modules/deploy switches to it within a minute,
# deferring only while drivers are racing and during the 03:00 blackout.
# Since the cutover (26 Sep 2026, ADR 0010) that edge reaches ARCADE-BOX:
# its agent gates the push and stages the rev, its homelab-deploy switches
# (ab21161: staged 13:47 CDT, switched 13:48). The Z840 has no agent, so a
# push here switches arcade-box only; the Z840 takes the same sha by hand,
# `nixos-rebuild switch --flake github:imkarrer/homelab/<sha>#llm-box`
# (docs/architecture.md Part III row 41, the accepted gap).
# DECISION on
# agent-push: "yes" means an agent pushing green IS switching the server.
# Decided "ask" at fd12f93 until the timer had been watched firing (row 21);
# flipped to "yes" 16 Sep 2026 by the operator, after the timer fired on its
# no-op path (13 Sep), the first staged closure switched by itself (14-15
# Sep), and all four trees reached the box unattended (agent-hub def0d6c in
# 80 s, home-arcade 789f994 via bump-lock 3db878b). The gate is still the
# gate: nothing is pushed red, and hub-status reads every build back.
# agent-push governs agents in WSL. CI's own bump-lock commits (scripts/
# hub-bump-lock.sh, triggered by ac-host's pipeline on green) are a different
# actor and are gated by HOMELAB_PUSH_TOKEN existing on the agent -- see
# docs/architecture.md Part III row 24. Both mean the same thing once the
# deploy unit is live: a push to homelab main is a system switch -- at 03:30
# when this was written, within a minute since ADR 0008, of arcade-box since
# the cutover.
homelab|/home/nixos/src/homelab|git@github.com:imkarrer/homelab|buildkite|yes
# agent-hub, home-arcade: deploy=environment since 18 Sep 2026 (homelab-158.11).
# Was `none` -- true only in the sense that no pipeline carried the tree to the
# Z840 directly; it reached it through homelab's closure when flake.lock
# moved (row 24). Now the tree's own green build is what reaches its host, one
# hop, and hub-status prints the staged/applied pair per tenant. Which host:
#   agent-hub   -> the Z840 (llm-box). No agent there since the cutover, so
#                  agent-hub-environment-poll on that host reads GitHub for a
#                  green sha (homelab-ygc.14) and agent-hub-environment-pull
#                  applies it. The status it reads, buildkite/agent-hub, has
#                  been published since 26 Sep 2026, 20:05 CDT; the poll's first
#                  live run staged and applied b16781d at 20:19 (architecture
#                  rows 35 and 40).
#   home-arcade -> arcade-box. queue-environment on arcade-box's agent stages
#                  the FloxHub generation; arcade-environment-pull applies it.
agent-hub|/home/nixos/src/agent-hub|git@github.com:imkarrer/agent-hub|environment|yes
home-arcade|/home/nixos/src/home-arcade|git@github.com:imkarrer/home-arcade|environment|yes
# bead-loop: deploy=none for either host -- the loop runs on the workstation and
# deploys itself by a pull (bead-loop systemd/bead-loop-deploy.timer); its pipeline
# only tests and automerges. Object: hub/pipelines/bead-loop.json (20 Sep 2026).
bead-loop|/home/nixos/src/bead-loop|git@github.com:imkarrer/bead-loop|none|yes
